EPISODE 8: "PROVOCATION"

Logline: Thalassia orchestrates a crisis to force Naël into the open—and he must choose between invisibility and saving lives.

Cold Open (Past Timeline — Age 18):
Naël, now an adult, applies for the marine-rescue certification. He is accepted. It is the first thing he has wanted in years. He does not tell his parents. He does not tell anyone. He simply begins training.

Main Title.

Act One (Present Timeline):
Thalassia orchestrates a maritime industrial crisis: a chemical spill with trapped workers. The location is chosen carefully—near enough to Sables-d'Or that Naël will hear about it, far enough that the rescue will be difficult and public.

Naël hears the news. He knows it is a trap. But he also knows that people will die if no one helps. The marine rescue team is deployed—but they will not arrive in time.

He must choose: remain invisible, or save lives in full daylight.

Act Two:
Yanis confronts Naël. He knows about the trap. He opposes it violently—but his opposition is not to the rescue. It is to the secrecy. "If you save them, they'll see you," he says. "And that's what Thalassia wants. But it's also what we need. Let them see. Let the world see."

Naël rejects this. "I'm not doing this for politics. I'm doing it because people are dying."

"Then do it for yourself," Yanis says. "Not for them. Not for me. For yourself."

The conflict is not hero vs. villain. It is two philosophies of visibility.

Flashback (Past Timeline — Age 11, Continued):
The growth lab, nine years ago. Young Naël touches the tank. The material reaches for him. But now we see something else: a moment of choice. The boy hesitates. He could pull back. He could run. But he does not. He watches the light approach his hand, and he lets it come.

The breach is not an accident. It is a decision.

Act Three:
Naël reveals himself partially in public for the first time. He uses his abilities to reach the trapped workers, his skin shifting to protect him from the chemicals and the cold. The rescue is successful. But it is also witnessed. Dozens of people see what he can do. Phones record. The footage spreads.

Vannier obtains irrefutable visual proof.

Léa sees the footage on the news. She recognizes the texture of the skin. She calls Naël. He does not answer.

Stinger:
Farah Ilan watches the footage. Her face is unreadable. "It's starting," she says quietly. "The endgame."

End of Episode.

