CONCLUSION

MIMESIS is not a superhero story. It is a story about what it means to be human when your body is no longer entirely yours. It is about the cost of hiding, the price of visibility, and the moment when acceptance becomes the only possible choice.

The season ends not with triumph but with being—the most radical state available to a character who has spent nine years disappearing. Naël does not become a hero. He becomes himself.

And that, in the end, is enough.

